    "nickname": "Ayush-Kukreti",
    "content": "In CodinGame, validators are hidden test cases used to verify that a solution works in all possible scenarios, not just the visible test cases provided in the problem. The key difference is that validators are similar but not identical to the test cases, ensuring that the solution isn't hardcoded specifically for the test cases. This helps to prevent players from tailoring their code to pass only the given test cases and ensures that their solutions are more general.\n\nValidators balance the test cases by covering edge cases and different inputs, but they aren't revealed to players during the coding process. The goal is to encourage solutions that work under a wide variety of conditions, rather than ones that rely on specific test cases​.\n\nAfter conducting research, I found a forum where developers and programmers discuss the many difficulties they face.\n\nPlease take this into consideration while approving:\nhttps://www.codingame.com/forum/t/clashofcode-contributions/197199",
    "codingamerHandle": "d2d376930a5cb70b4e473f190bb5a5f46673726",
    "avatar": 154782329914859,
    "elapsedTime": 59345560000
  },
