    "nickname": "Anastaszor",
    "content": "Hi,\n\nMy first attempt has a code that matches all of the given tests but missed (only) the last validator. This is a problem because the coder will think its algo may work when it's not the case.\n\nThe problem was the sort was comparing numbers char after char, and missed those two in the last validator :\n\n  46 => '1170',\n  47 => '11708',\n\nSuch configuration where 2 numbers have the same digits until some point, but where their concatenation is in reverse order than all of the other configurations in the tests (like 9 and 90 , where it is always preferable to have the shortest number first) must be on the test suite, and in an easy to spot test.\n\nAs an example, could you add in your test suite something like :\n\nInput :\n2\n123    12\nOutput :\n12312\n(test larger number first)\n\nInput :\n2\n281   28\nOutput :\n28281\n(test smaller number first)\n\nGiven the logic it should not be hard to find corresponding validators.\n\nThank you",
    "codingamerHandle": "7a12217e7f22d69c67bb1ffa7a9818c64445875",
